# Copy to .env and fill in. Every variable is read only in
# adapters/config.go, and validated there.

# dev or prod. In dev, .env.local and .env are loaded; in prod, neither.
APP_ENV=dev
PORT=8080

# Neon. The DIRECT connection is preferred over the pooled one: pgx keeps
# a prepared statement cache per connection, which transaction pooling
# breaks. `neon init` writes both into .env.local.
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# A throwaway database for the repository tests. They skip without it,
# and they create and drop their own rows, so never point this at the
# real pantry.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# The bot (cmd/api). The Anthropic key lives in `fly secrets` and never
# in the local shell profile: an exported key makes Claude Code stop
# using the subscription and bill the key instead.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Default claude-opus-5-5. What matters is the quality of portion
# estimates, so start high and measure before going cheaper.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# The tool-use cap for one message, default 6. A runaway loop is a bug,
# not an expense — this is what keeps it from being both.
BOT_MAX_TOOL_ITERATIONS=

# WhatsApp Cloud API. The allowed list is closed: anyone who can send a
# message can write to the pantry. Comma separated, any formatting —
# only the digits are compared.
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_ALLOWED_NUMBERS=
# Phase D: the approved utility template the weekly digest goes out as.
WHATSAPP_DIGEST_TEMPLATE=
